three new mobs have been announced for  minecraft for fans to vote on during  minecraft live this weekend battlefield  2042 has revealed its brand new game  mode hazard zone and all of the  competitive playlist details for halo  infinite have been revealed i'm persia  and this is your gamespot news  minecraft live is right around the  corner and after releasing each mob one  by one throughout the entire week we now  know which mobs we get to vote on during  the show each mob has its own bit of  utility that opens new possibilities the  first mob is the glare which can spot  dark areas nearby and flies directly to  them to notify you of potential places  dangerous mods will spawn the light  levels required for mobs to spawn will  be changing in the next update of  minecraft mobs will now require a light  level of zero to spawn which means you  will need a lot fewer torches or light  sources to keep your base safe having a  glare could help you scout out any dark  areas you may have missed while spawn  proofing the alley is a cute flying  friend who will gather items for you  that match whatever item you give it  this mob also loves music and will  deliver the collected items to the  nearest noteblock mini theories around  this friendly looking vex revolve around  its potential usefulness in delivering  items to your storage easy collection  for semi-automatic farms and more for  those who love to sink their time into  mega bases this little friend may be  exactly what you need to help gather all  of those loose blocks that you mine for  your build when your inventory is full  and the third mob is the copper golem  this cute little golem also means the  addition of copper buttons in the reveal  trailer it's noted that the copper golem  loves to press these buttons randomly  which leaves open many creative  opportunities just like copper blocks  the golem will oxidize over time  freezing up after a certain stage it's  unclear if we'll be able to wax them to  prevent this or not just yet but we'll  definitely know more soon all three of  these mobs are super interesting to me  and have so much utility in their own  right i can only imagine how much more  intricate redstone contraptions and  autofarms will become with one of these  mobs on the way which mob are you gonna  be voting for make sure you let me know  in the comments and of course tune in  this saturday because we're gonna be  streaming it right here on our channel  too  ea and dice have officially announced  battlefield 2042's new hazard zone game  mode in hazard zone you play in a four  member squad and your objective is to  locate and retrieve data drives that  have fallen from satellites you'll scour  the landscape for these drives as you  fight against ai combatants and other  teams of human players trying to do the  same thing dai says hazard zone is not a  battle royale mode as the objective is  not strictly to kill other players but  to escape with as many drives as  possible there are gonna be two time  limited extraction opportunities during  the match and the extraction points are  located on two different parts of the  map you and your team can opt to leave  during the first extraction which  happens midway through the match or wait  until the end of the final extraction  it's riskier to wait but you also have  more time to collect drives so the  rewards will be greater in any event  only two squads will make it out alive  or none no matter what only one player  on the team needs to survive and extract  for the entire team to win hazard zone  supports 24 players on ps4 and xbox one  and 32 players on ps5 xbox series xns  and pc so six to eight teams of four  depending on your platform hazard zone  uses all seven maps from battlefield  2042's all out warfare mode and another  thing to note is that each squad cannot  have more than one of the same  specialist character also players who  are killed can be brought back into the  match through a revive system your team  can purchase speaking of purchase hazard  zone has a metagame element too drives  have values assigned to them and  collecting the drives gives you access  to hazards on specific currency called  dark market credits these credits can be  spent to acquire weapons gadgets and  upgrades before matches and honestly  this just scratches the surface of what  hazard zone is all about we have a full  breakdown on everything that it has to  offer on our channel right now courtesy  of our very own david ahmadi so check  that out if you want to know more  a few technical previews have passed and  we've gotten a good look at the social  playlists but 343 has now revealed all  of the competitive settings for halo  infinite i honestly had one simple wish  going into this reveal and it was  granted immediately with br start i know  many players like to have variety and  use as many different weapons as  possible but the br holds a special  place in my heart and i'm happy to see  it back as a starting weapon however  there is no secondary so you will have  to scavenge for a backup when you can  other major changes from the social  playlists will be the removal of the  motion tracker and friendly fire being  on so be careful of those needs weapons  equipment and grenades on maps will  always appear in the same location on  each map and mode combination and will  respawn at the same intervals this is  definitely a classic halo pvp feel that  is going to require teamwork  communication and rotations to set up  for power weapons to succeed in terms of  hit markers only ones for grenades are  set to be disabled in competitive the  modes will include slayer capture the  flag strongholds and oddball for lots  lots more check out 343's in-depth blog  post that runs through everything you  need to know about halo infinite  competitive and if you want even more  competitive halo news well the first in  person halo infinite tournament takes  place in raleigh north carolina this  december and tickets sold out almost  immediately  so many new things are on the way for  these franchises that we love and have  loved for a long time minecraft  battlefield halo do you remember the  first time you ever played these games  and did you ever expect to see them  where they are now let me know in the  comments and of course make sure you  subscribe so you don't miss your next  gamespot news update  [Music]  [Music]  foreign
 

